upstream_license: AGPL-3.0
upstream_title: Goldbach30 / Goldbach29 FRACTRAN reduction pair and Goldbach29 halting semantics

attribution_boundary:
  Mike Dupont / meta-introspector owns the upstream Goldbach30 and Goldbach29
  constructions, their 30-to-29 fraction reduction, abstract machines,
  FRACTRAN programs, Lean proofs fstep_enc, and the later source-visible Lean
  theorem goldbachProg_halts_iff.
  DASHI owns only this provenance receipt plus its independent observer/fibre
  translation, exact arithmetic reconstruction of the success macro, and
  DASHI-native consumer/cost theorems built from that explicitly attributed
  external fact surface.

external_facts_used:
  - Goldbach30 has 30 fractions and 11 control states
  - Goldbach29 has 29 fractions and 10 control states
  - the first 25 annotated rules are shared before the success/failure tail
  - the SA control state is removed in Goldbach29
  - Goldbach30 success uses NT.B -> SA, the SA/SB transfer loop, then SA -> RA.A
  - Goldbach29 success reroutes the transfer through NT.B/SB, stages through
    NT2.B, and reuses the existing NT.B b c -> RA.A transition
  - each Program.lean proves one encoded FRACTRAN step matches one abstract
    astep step (fstep_enc)
  - at semantic_source_revision, Goldbach29/Main.lean contains theorem
    goldbachProg_halts_iff: the 29-fraction program halts from N0 iff there is
    an even n >= 4 with no representation as a sum of two primes

path_provenance_note:
  The construction commit itself records Goldbach29 under the d3e01240 UUID
  directory. A later/user-supplied link used another UUID path; DASHI does not
  rewrite commit-native provenance to that later path.

non_claims:
  - this receipt does not vendor-copy AGPL source into DASHI
  - this receipt does not claim DASHI authorship of Goldbach30 or Goldbach29
  - imported Lean theorem authority is not an Agda proof
  - goldbachProg_halts_iff is an equivalence to a counterexample; it is not a
    proof that no counterexample exists and therefore does not prove Goldbach
  - this receipt alone does not prove Goldbach30/29 whole-machine weak bisimulation
